From 1f29c15cc0f40208b194f927077beb7065e1e0d1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: adbtrr_work6_sched_tc_fixed <>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 19:27:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] apps/examples/testcase: add randomised soak scenario

Phase 6, and the last of the scenario test rollout.

Every other scenario sets up one arrangement and checks one outcome.  That
is what makes them diagnostic, and it is also their limit: they only ever
visit the states somebody thought to write down.  The soak does the
opposite, running a long sequence of randomised workloads that vary task
count, priority spread and affinity, and checking the same small set of
invariants after each round.  It is not trying to localise a defect; it is
trying to reach a state no fixed scenario would.

The starvation monitor runs throughout, so a violation is attributed to the
round that produced it.  On failure the round's full parameters are printed,
worker by worker, which is usually enough to turn a soak failure into a
reproducible fixed scenario.  The generator is deliberately deterministic
and its seed is printed at the start, because a soak failure is only useful
if the sequence can be replayed.

Fairness is only asserted for rounds where every worker happened to share a
priority, since that is the only arrangement in which equal shares are the
correct outcome, and the threshold is looser than the dedicated round-robin
scenarios use because a soak round is shorter and its masks are arbitrary.

The soak has its own Kconfig symbol separate from the rest of the scenario
tier, so that enabling the scenarios does not silently enable a run lasting
minutes.  Duration is configurable and defaults to sixty seconds; the
catalogue figure for a nightly job is 1800.

Both the SMP and non-SMP compilation paths are warning free under -Wall
-Wextra.
---
 apps/examples/testcase/le_tc/kernel/Kconfig   |  22 ++
 apps/examples/testcase/le_tc/kernel/Make.defs |   3 +
 .../testcase/le_tc/kernel/kernel_tc_main.c    |   4 +
 .../testcase/le_tc/kernel/stc_sched_soak.c    | 338 ++++++++++++++++++
 .../testcase/le_tc/kernel/tc_internal.h       |   1 +
 5 files changed, 368 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 apps/examples/testcase/le_tc/kernel/stc_sched_soak.c

diff --git a/apps/examples/testcase/le_tc/kernel/Kconfig b/apps/examples/testcase/le_tc/kernel/Kconfig
index 6dcea0c2..c57aef95 100644
--- a/apps/examples/testcase/le_tc/kernel/Kconfig
+++ b/apps/examples/testcase/le_tc/kernel/Kconfig
@@ -272,5 +272,27 @@ config STC_KERNEL_SCHED
 		selected by TC_KN_ALL; enable them for a nightly or on demand run
 		rather than for a per commit gate.
 
+config STC_KERNEL_SCHED_SOAK
+	bool "STC Sched soak (long running)"
+	default n
+	depends on STC_KERNEL_SCHED
+	---help---
+		Randomised mixed workload soak for the scheduler.
+
+		This runs for minutes rather than seconds and is intended for a
+		nightly job, not for an interactive run.  It varies task count,
+		priority spread and affinity on every round and checks the same
+		invariants after each, so it reaches combinations that the fixed
+		scenarios do not enumerate.
+
+config STC_SCHED_SOAK_SECONDS
+	int "Soak duration in seconds"
+	default 60
+	depends on STC_KERNEL_SCHED_SOAK
+	---help---
+		Total wall clock duration of the soak.  The catalogue figure for
+		a nightly run is 1800.  The default is deliberately short so
+		that enabling the soak by accident does not stall a run.
+
 endif #EXAMPLES_TESTCASE_KERNEL
 
